WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.520
You'd like the fish.

2
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.870
In French, that's «poisson».

3
00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:06.690
Make one small slip in
the middle of that word,

4
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.120
and you've just asked for «poison».

5
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.110
Then there's «hôpital».

6
00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:13.220
The H is right there on the page,

7
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:14.890
but you won't hear it.

8
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:17.660
Why does French write
a letter it won't say?

9
00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:20.830
And which other spellings
catch English speakers out?

10
00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:23.830
In this mission, you'll
drive the letters C and G

11
00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.600
down a two-lane road.

12
00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:29.710
Then you'll sort tricky letters
by ear into five buckets.

13
00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:33.620
Your mission: work out which French
letters say what they look like,

14
00:00:33.620 --> 00:00:34.770
and which ones don't.
